                <pb facs="0801" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg715"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. McCormick,.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: To enable the Department to answer several
                    inquiries it has received I shall be pleased if you will ascertain whether
                    Jewish divorces granted by Jewish rabbis are recognized by Russian law. If such
                    a law is in force a translation of its text is desired.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
